# Ordinal map -- Xbox kernel ordinal -> the symbol that implements it.
#
# xb/gen-exports.py reads this together with nxdk's xboxkrnl.exe.def.  A
# mapped ordinal's export-directory entry points at the named symbol; an
# unmapped ordinal resolves to a generated, arity-correct, self-naming
# bugcheck stub.  The signature (calling convention + argument bytes) always
# comes from xboxkrnl.exe.def, so the named symbol must match that ABI.
#
# Line syntax:
#   <ord>  <symbol>                          mapped to <symbol>
#   <ord>  <symbol>  <internal_name>         mapped, asm symbol differs
#                                            (spec2def 'name() _internal' form)
#   <ord>  =<value>                          unmapped DATA scaffold; override
#                                            the default (zero) initializer
#   <ord>                                    unmapped; reserves a slot just to
#                                            carry the inline `# comment` into
#                                            the spec (useful TODO markers)
# Any line may carry a trailing `# free-form note`, which the generator
# appends in parentheses to the spec's `; <xboxkrnl_name>` annotation.

# --- Av display subsystem ------------------------------------------------- #
1    AvGetSavedDataAddress            # no saved framebuffer on a cold boot
2    AvSendTVEncoderOption            # TV-encoder query / control
3    AvSetDisplayMode                 # point the NV2A CRTC at the framebuffer
4    AvSetSavedDataAddress

